Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; =====================================================================
;  SubSell fleet policy (Windows / Chrome)
;  Extension ID: jdbjbonhdnfkkfihbodmhpmccoiajflm
;
;  What this does on a machine:
;   1) Force-installs SubSell from your self-hosted update.xml (auto-updates).
;   2) Points it at your shared settings file (configUrl) so the API key +
;      settings arrive automatically — nothing to type on the machine.
;
;  BEFORE deploying, replace the two placeholders below:
;   - YOUR-HOST                -> where you host subsell.crx + update.xml
;   - the configUrl gist link  -> your secret gist raw URL (holds the settings)
;
;  Apply: double-click this file (or push it with your GPO/MDM/RMM), then
;  fully restart Chrome. Verify at chrome://policy and chrome://extensions.
; =====================================================================

; --- 1) Force-install + auto-update -----------------------------------
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\ExtensionInstallForcelist]
"1"="jdbjbonhdnfkkfihbodmhpmccoiajflm;https://YOUR-HOST/subsell/update.xml"

; --- 2) Central config (the key + settings) ---------------------------
; EASY (recommended): point at your secret gist raw URL. Edit the gist later
; and every machine follows. Nothing else to escape.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\3rdparty\extensions\jdbjbonhdnfkkfihbodmhpmccoiajflm\policy]
"configUrl"="https://gist.githubusercontent.com/USER/GIST_ID/raw/subsell-config.json"

; ADVANCED (no gist): instead of configUrl, push the whole settings inline as
; one escaped JSON string. Delete the configUrl line above and use this:
; "configJson"="{\"apiKey\":\"sk-ant-REPLACE\",\"businessName\":\"...\",\"priceList\":\"...\"}"
